  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1001.01 Applicability",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1001.01 Applicability. This chapter shall govern the expenditure of money from the hazardous waste cleanup fund (HWCF) for the following purposes:\n\n(a) To respond to the discharge of hazardous waste;\n\n(b) To develop a state hazardous waste facility siting program;\n\n(c) To encourage and facilitate the implementation of household hazardous waste (HHW) collection projects, as described herein; and\n\n(d) To encourage and facilitate the collection of household do-it-yourself (DIY) used oil by household DIY used oil collection centers.\n\nSource. #5053, eff 1-24-91; ss by #5886, eff 8-26-94; ss by #7333, eff 8-1-00; ss by #9215, INTERIM, eff 8-1-08; ss by #9367, eff 1-28-09; ss by #12352, eff 8-14-17; ss by #14284, eff 8-1-25, EXPIRES: 8-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1000.html"
